    "text": "A permutation of Z is called residue-class-wise affine if there is a positive\ninteger m such that its restrictions to the residue classes (mod m) are all affine.\nIs CT(Z) the group of all residue-class-wise affine permutations of Z which fix the\nnonnegative integers setwise?                                               S. Kohl",
